{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$H^0(U, \\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$I$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{M/I^nM\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{H^0(U, \\mathcal{F}_n)\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$A$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\mathcal{G}_n = \\widetilde{M/I^n M}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$M$", "MATH_0009": "$I$", "MATH_0010": "$A$", "MATH_0011": "$M/I^n M$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-canonically-algebraizable}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-finite-over-complete-ring}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b7bf2f85fb84a4ee2acc5f5be7f2b1f3f90ba41b0e37e2c7b3624d7faea816f8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:359ccf5b9a1924f86a992f93cf6937e30280c25a40555d74e36b01cd2e8aaa1b", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> has the Mittag-Leffler condition\nand since the limit topology on <MATH_0002> is the <MATH_0003>-adic topology\nwe see that <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>\nare pro-isomorphic inverse systems of <MATH_0006>-modules.\nThus if we set\n<MATH_0007>\nthen we see that to verify the condition in\nDefinition <REF_0001>\nit suffices to show that <MATH_0008> is a finite module over the\n<MATH_0009>-adic completion of <MATH_0010>. This follows from\nthe fact that <MATH_0011> is finite by condition (c)\nand the above and\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f0e8445617f6ddb08dba3a6196e7829c44a1c5975605be639a2853d9eb98d47c", "unit_id": "tag:0EHH:proof"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-when-done}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:32132474caac26fafb413c2bfa24dfd994753e381a341abdc1b112a77505104c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following is in some sense the most straightforward possible application\nLemma <REF_0001> above.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06825bd2af68cafe2903b6af0349e944b313771ac1ea536d97e358dd5e0a50b9", "unit_id": "tag:0DXS:prose-0008"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DXS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Coh}(U, I\\mathcal{O}_U)$", "MATH_0003": "$I = (f)$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\in \\mathfrak a$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}_n$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_U/f^n\\mathcal{O}_U$", "MATH_0007": "$H^1_\\mathfrak a(A/fA)$", "MATH_0008": "$H^2_\\mathfrak a(A/fA)$", "MATH_0009": "$A$", "MATH_0010": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$A$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\mathcal{F}_n)$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{O}_U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-algebraize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-algebraization-principal-variant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fa4bc7efebc30a842315c6a52ddbfa661baf20b9641f32417912011dce18f67f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ce0941010d172d35bc665b5c0530c044e403c97f929c6184fc7654e450953b4", "source_text": "In Situation <REF_0001> let\n<MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002>.\nAssume\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is a principal ideal for a nonzerodivisor <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is a finite locally free\n<MATH_0006>-module,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008>\nare finite <MATH_0009>-modules.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen <MATH_0010> extends canonically to <MATH_0011>. In particular, if <MATH_0012>\nis complete, then <MATH_0013> is the completion of a coherent\n<MATH_0014>-module.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8872c988d940c32f49ca6c3ce34de659976ca3a5d5f0c05b45ee93a0058b5207", "unit_id": "tag:0DXW:statement"}
